language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ initials_queue: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ I noticed something weird about names of the first 10 people in the queue for a Maths lecture.
$ Each of them had initials which were an alphabetically ordered pair of distinct letters from the
$ first five letters of the alphabet (A, B, C, D, E). None of the people had the same initials as
$ any other and no-one shared a letter with the person in front of them. Mathematician BE was at
$ the front of the queue with CD right behind, while BD was right at the end of the queue. Work
$ out the initials of the ten people in the queue, starting from the front.
$
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/initials_queue.html
$ Save this model as model.eprime and run it with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the solution is
$ written to `model.eprime.solution`:
$   savilerow model.eprime -run-solver

$ the number of people in the queue
letting people = 10
$ the number of letters, A to E
letting letters = 5

$ queue[i,1], queue[i,2]: the first and second initial of the person i-th in the queue, from the front (the letters A to E as 0 to letters-1)
find queue : matrix indexed by [int(1..people), int(1..2)] of int(0..letters-1)
$ code[i]: the initials of person i as letters * first + second, so that two people with the same initials have the same code
find code : matrix indexed by [int(1..people)] of int(0..letters*letters-1)

such that
$ each person's initials are an alphabetically ordered pair of distinct letters
forAll i : int(1..people) . queue[i,1] < queue[i,2],
$ the code of each person
forAll i : int(1..people) . code[i] = letters * queue[i,1] + queue[i,2],
$ no two people have the same initials
allDiff(code),
$ the person at the front has initials BE
queue[1,1] = 1 /\ queue[1,2] = 4,
$ the person right behind the front has initials CD
queue[2,1] = 2 /\ queue[2,2] = 3,
$ the person at the end of the queue has initials BD
queue[people,1] = 1 /\ queue[people,2] = 3,
$ nobody shares a letter with the person in front of them
forAll i : int(1..people-1) . (queue[i,1] != queue[i+1,1] /\ queue[i,1] != queue[i+1,2] /\ queue[i,2] != queue[i+1,1] /\ queue[i,2] != queue[i+1,2])
